      {
        "id": 2100824471,
        "content": "###### Draft\r\nThere's several properties we must associate with issues in the context of displaying them correctly. \r\n1. `origin` - where the issue was loaded from `localStorage | octokit`\r\n   - Any `octokit` origin issue (freshly loaded from the API) should have a visual indicator as being \"new\"\r\n2. `fullIssueId` - we only load issue previews from `@ubiquity/devpool-directory/issues` and we need to associate the preview issue ID to the \"full\" issue ID that it points to. \r\n- I also think that we should immediately display from cache first, and then fetch updates in the background. \r\n- If an issue is no longer present according to octokit, we need to sync our localStorage (remove the issue) so that it does not display anymore.",
        "url": "https://github.com/ubiquity/work.ubq.fi/issues/6",
